        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A fixed-length byte array of 10 bytes consisting of 40 2-bit fields.</para>
<para>Only the first 37 fields are used by channel classification. The nth field (numbering from 0) contains the classification value of data channel index n. Classification is defined as following values:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Value 0: Unknown</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Value 1: Good</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Value 3: Bad </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
